The Usual Speed Traps
Oversized image files
JavaScript and CSS that block rendering
Absent CDN or caching layer
Too many tracking scripts and widgets
Unoptimized custom fonts
Testing exclusively on desktop
Fixes That Actually Move the Needle
Compress images and use next-gen formats
Defer scripts that aren't immediately needed
Use a CDN to shorten delivery distance
Set fixed dimensions for media to avoid shifting
Remove underperforming third-party tools
Check real user metrics regularly
Quick FAQ
Q.1 Is a fast site guaranteed to rank well? 
No but it removes a real barrier that could otherwise hold back an otherwise strong page. 
Q.2 What load time should I aim for? 
Under 2.5 seconds for LCP; total load under 3 seconds is ideal. 
Q.3 Are speed fixes a one-time job? 
No — performance needs regular monitoring as content, scripts, and traffic evolve.
